<title>UK: Tesco chief resigns from NatWest board.</title>
<headline>Tesco chief resigns from NatWest board.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Westminster Group said on Thursday that Lord MacLaurin, the chairman of Tesco Plc, had resigned from the group's board after the British retail chain announced plans to develop its own retail banking network.</p>
<p>Lord MacLaurin was on the board of NatWest since 1990.</p>
<p>Tesco announced earlier on Thursday that it had agreed on a financial services joint venture with the Royal Bank of Scotland.</p>
<p>The venture would launch an internationally accepted credit card and also offer telebanking services.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
